      "side": 1,
      "message": "`mServiceUuids` is shared between encrypted and not encrypted data.\nI see 2 problems with that:\n1. It make it impossible to have both encrypted and not encrypted serviceUuid in the same advertising. I understand that this capability should remain, let me know if I am wrong\n\n2. The last caller of the builder will override the encryption state. It will be errorprone for app developper and they will have to look at the code implementation to fix it\n\n\nMaybe a better API would be (pseudo-code without any check):\n```\npublic Builder addServiceUuid(ParcelUuid serviceUuid) {  \n   mServiceUuids.add(serviceUuid);\n}\npublic Builder addServiceUuidEnc(ParcelUuid serviceUuid) {  \n   mServiceUuidsEnc.add(serviceUuid);\n}\n```\n\nThis comment apply for all other API that take user data",
